```

## Error Handling

The `getPostsV2` function will throw an error if the cursor is not found. You can handle this error in your application logic:

```ts
try {
  const posts = await getPostsV2(parseInt(id), limit)
  return NextResponse.json(posts)
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof Error && error.message.includes('cursor')) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Cursor not found' }, { status: 404 })
  }
  return NextResponse.json({ error: 'Failed to fetch posts' }, { status: 500 })
}
```

