## Extending Prisma Client

Prisma Client extensions are called extenders. You can use them to add additional functionality to your models, input types, and output types. 
Learn more about extenders in Prisma Client
.

### Extending the client model

To extend the Prisma Client model, you can use the 
`model`
 extension function to extend a 
`User`
 model.

The 
`model`
 extension function takes two arguments:

- `name`: The name of the model.

- `id`: The unique identifier of the model.

Here's an example of how to extend the 
`User`
 model:

```
import { PrismaClient, User } from "@prisma/client";

const prisma = new PrismaClient().$extends({
  model: {
    user: { ... },
  },
});

type MyUser = User & {
  posts: { title: string };
};

